        "original_id": "ecb57a4d-57f5-5487-9d96-c8a6deddf3a7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mark Romanek, Johnny Cash, Madonna, Michael Jackson, Janet Jackson\n- Bands/Artists: Nine Inch Nails, Red Hot Chili Peppers, Curve, Love and Rockets, Placebo, Massive Attack, Boards of Canada\n- Songs: \"The Hand That Feeds\", \"Closer\", \"Hurt\", \"Can't Stop\", \"Bedtime Story\", \"Scream\"\n- Albums: The Downward Spiral\n- Films: We\n- Charts: Billboard Hot 100\n- Topics: crossover hits, pop radio, music videos, film music\n\nFacts:\n- \"Closer\" is a 1994 song by American industrial rock band Nine Inch Nails from their second studio album The Downward Spiral.\n- Nine Inch Nails had top 40 radio hits with \"Closer\" in 1994 and \"Hurt\" in 1995.\n- Mark Romanek's notable music videos include Nine Inch Nails' \"Closer,\" Johnny Cash's \"Hurt,\" Red Hot Chili Peppers' \"Can't Stop,\" Madonna's \"Bedtime Story,\" and Michael and Janet Jackson's \"Scream.\"\n- Nine Inch Nails' \"The Hand That Feeds\" was a crossover hit that crossed over to pop radio and peaked at number 31 on the Billboard Hot 100.\n- The film We combines the speech \"Come September\" with varied video footage and music, mostly electronica and industrial, including music by Curve, Nine Inch Nails, Love and Rockets, Placebo, Massive Attack, and Boards of Canada.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
